 "relevance_note": "Retrospective cohort of 37 VEOIBD patients in which 'The frequent mutations were found in TNFAIP3 (n=5)'; the five TNFAIP3 patients are reported only in aggregate, except one described individually in the Figure 4 legend ('(D-F) Another patient with TNFAIP3 mutations').",
 "method_note": "Read the whole paper by hand; no script transcribed any table (Table 1 is aggregate VCE lesion counts by monogenic vs non-monogenic group, with no per-patient rows, so it was not extracted). Patient-level data are said to be in Table S1, which is supplementary and absent from the full text. Five patients with TNFAIP3 mutations are reported, but only one is described individually: the Figure 4 legend, panels D-F. I emitted rows for her only, labelled with the paper's own phrase 'Another patient with TNFAIP3 mutations', and did not create placeholder rows for the other four, who have no label, no variant description and no individually attributable features. Sex 'female' rests on the pronoun 'her' in that legend. 'small lesions' is recorded as printed (in context probably small-bowel lesions on VCE). No variant description, zygosity or inheritance is printed for any TNFAIP3 patient; the variants row records the gene only, with variant_original_string 'not reported'. Pathogenicity 'identified pathogenic variants' comes from the Figure 1 legend, which the text cites for the TNFAIP3 (n=5) count. Count statements not attributed to her because the paper does not say which patients they cover: 'All patients with TNFAIP3 mutations except one suffered from ileal ulcers'; Figure 2 (G,H) 'Multiple ulcers and erosions found in two patients with TNFAIP3 mutations'; '4 (10.8%) patients had recurrent infections'; cohort-level treatments. 'Patients with TNFAIP3 mutations also had colonic erosions and ulcers identified by colonoscopy' names the group, so it is recorded as observed with evidence_basis 'inferred from group statement'. Not recorded for her: onset before 6 years (only the VEOIBD definition in the Introduction), country (the study was run in China, but her origin is not stated), vital status. Possible prior report: the paper says 'Our prior work described phenotype and genotype of VEOIBD patients, and patients with certain monogenic defects (7,8)' and, citing ref. 30 (a TNFAIP3 infantile-onset IBD paper), 'Previous studies showed that these patients had ulcers'; it does not state that its own TNFAIP3 patients were reported before, so cites_prior_report_of_same_patients is null. Internal inconsistencies: 58 VCE procedures stated vs Table 1 total n=55 (26 monogenic + 29 non-monogenic); monogenic IBD in '18 patients (48.6%)' in Results vs '45% of patients had monogenic IBD' in Discussion. evidence_basis cells reuse the status span.",
